COMPILATION OF: E46N8

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E46N8

   1 a 0000 E46N8:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-42/P2c] THE ROUTING CONTRAST, INSIDE ONE OBJECT.
   4 a 0006      A console `put skip;' (REVERSE:00FE, 17 bytes, ends
   5 a 0006      in ?SYSPR) and a file `put file(outf) skip;'
   6 a 0006      (CREATE:41, 20 bytes, ends in ?SIOOP then ?QIOOP) in
   7 a 0006      the SAME program.  The current matcher takes its
   8 a 0006      bare-control arm BEFORE it looks at the FILE option
   9 a 0006      and tests the STREAM option first, so it sends the
  10 a 0006      FILE one to ?SYSPR.  This object is the witness that
  11 a 0006      says whether the implementation kept them apart: the
  12 a 0006      console one must reach ?SYSPR and the file one must
  13 a 0006      NOT. */
  14 c 0006   dcl outf file;
  15 c 0006   open file(outf) stream output title('N8OUT DAT');
  16 c 0023   put skip;
  17 c 0034   put file(outf) skip;
  18 c 0048   close file(outf);
  19 a 004E end E46N8;

CODE SIZE = 0051
DATA AREA = 0009
FREE SYMS = 38B3
END  COMPILATION
